WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.000
TypeScript-style upgrades

00:00:01.895 --> 00:00:02.802
but for C

00:00:03.342 --> 00:00:04.827
Type-C is C11

00:00:04.639 --> 00:00:05.334
with the types

00:00:05.146 --> 00:00:06.007
C is missing

00:00:06.208 --> 00:00:07.316
variants checked by

00:00:07.127 --> 00:00:07.823
match

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:09.026
distinct types for

00:00:08.837 --> 00:00:10.110
ids and units

00:00:10.182 --> 00:00:11.773
generics and errors

00:00:11.585 --> 00:00:12.528
as values

00:00:13.054 --> 00:00:14.327
Its compiler takes

00:00:14.139 --> 00:00:15.223
the same command

00:00:15.035 --> 00:00:16.179
line as cc

00:00:16.344 --> 00:00:17.523
turns Type-C into

00:00:17.346 --> 00:00:18.266
readable C

00:00:18.384 --> 00:00:19.245
and hands that

00:00:19.056 --> 00:00:19.846
to your normal

00:00:19.658 --> 00:00:20.660
C compiler

00:00:21.182 --> 00:00:22.667
Every C11 file

00:00:22.491 --> 00:00:23.575
is already valid

00:00:23.387 --> 00:00:24.094
Type-C

00:00:24.201 --> 00:00:25.167
so a project

00:00:24.979 --> 00:00:25.816
can adopt it

00:00:25.628 --> 00:00:26.394
one file at

00:00:26.206 --> 00:00:26.889
a time

00:00:27.028 --> 00:00:28.219
It's early with

00:00:28.031 --> 00:00:28.667
much of the

00:00:28.479 --> 00:00:30.070
language still unbuilt

00:00:30.606 --> 00:00:31.620
Full story on

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:32.327
the dashboard
